REVIEW PROBE (pre-existing hazard, unchanged by this change)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
isMissingLaunchAgent matches the substring "113" anywhere in the launchctl error text, and
runLaunchctl formats that text as `launchctl <args>: <output>` where <args> contains
`gui/<uid>/works.relux.mac-infra-browser-heartbeat.<name>`. A temporary probe test proved a
genuine failure is misclassified:

  launchctl bootout gui/501/works.relux.mac-infra-browser-heartbeat.hb113:
  Operation not permitted while System Integrity Protection is engaged
  -> isMissingLaunchAgent() == true

Heartbeat names match [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,47}, so `hb113` is legal; a uid containing 113 has the
same effect. Identical helper exists at base (fa43cb3:internal/browsersession/heartbeat.go:777),
so this is not a regression, but expire() is a new caller that removes the plist and state
BEFORE bootout, so a swallowed genuine failure leaves a loaded KeepAlive job with no plist
(throttled respawn until logout) instead of returning an error.
